# Cisco RoomOS xAPI Driver (HTTPS /putxml + /getxml)
#
# Controls Cisco Webex video-conferencing endpoints over the RoomOS xAPI.
# Standby, audio, microphones, dial / hangup, do-not-disturb, presentation,
# camera presets, on-screen messaging, and reboot — the AV-integrator
# essentials surface, not a wrap of the entire xAPI.
#
# Models covered:
#   The xAPI is identical across the entire current Webex / RoomOS family —
#   one driver covers all of:
#     - Codec Pro, Codec Plus, Codec EQ
#     - Room Bar, Room Bar Pro
#     - Room Kit, Room Kit Mini, Room Kit EQ, Room Kit EQX
#     - Room 55, Room 55 Dual, Room 70, Room 70 G2, Room 70 Single G2,
#       Room 70 Dual G2, Room Panorama, Room 70 Panorama
#     - Board Pro 55 / 75, Board Pro G2
#     - Desk, Desk Mini, Desk Pro
#
# Protocol reference:
#   Cisco RoomOS 11 API Reference Guide (D15502.11, RoomOS 11.27, 05-2025) —
#   https://www.cisco.com/c/dam/en/us/td/docs/telepresence/endpoint/roomos-1127/api-reference-guide-roomos-1127.pdf
#   (browsable form: https://roomos.cisco.com/print/TechDocs/HttpApi)
#   Two HTTPS endpoints on port 443:
#     GET  /getxml?location=/Status/...     — read xStatus / xConfiguration tree
#     POST /putxml  (Content-Type: text/xml) — execute xCommand or set
#                                              xConfiguration via XML body
#
# Push vs. poll:
#   Push via HttpFeedback (the codec's webhook mechanism): on connect the
#   driver registers OpenAVC's callback URL on one of the codec's four
#   feedback slots (xCommand HttpFeedback Register) with XPath expressions
#   covering the polled status paths. The codec then POSTs the changed
#   xStatus subtree as XML the moment it changes, and the body feeds the
#   same response rules as a poll reply. Polling stays on as the resync
#   baseline (30 s), and the registration repeats in each poll cycle —
#   re-registering is idempotent and re-activates a slot the codec
#   deactivated after failed deliveries (the xCommand HttpFeedback Enable
#   case in the API guide).
#
#   Feedback bodies wrap the changed node with item="1" attributes and an
#   <Identification> block (SystemName / MACAddress / SerialNumber / ...) —
#   the response rules below are attribute-tolerant and anchored so the
#   Identification fields never shadow the payload (the serial rule requires
#   the SystemUnit poll's <Module> parent on purpose).
#
#   Status polling is leaf-level (one getxml location per state variable):
#   response dispatch applies the first matching rule per body, so a broad
#   /Status/Audio body could only ever update one of volume / output mute /
#   mic mute per poll. One location per value makes every poll body — and
#   every push body, which arrives leaf-shaped anyway — hit exactly its rule.
#
# Authentication:
#   Username and password are supplied in the Add Device dialog. A codec
#   user with the Admin role (the default "admin" user qualifies) enables
#   everything, including push feedback registration — xCommand HttpFeedback
#   Register requires ADMIN per the API guide. An Integrator-role user can
#   still control the codec fully, but the feedback registration is refused,
#   leaving state updates at poll speed. xConfiguration writes are not
#   included either way (settings live in the Cisco web UI, not the AV
#   control surface).

id: cisco_roomos_xapi
name: Cisco Webex Codec / Room Series (xAPI)
manufacturer: Cisco
category: video
version: 1.3.0
author: OpenAVC
description: >
  Controls Cisco Webex video-conferencing endpoints (Codec Pro / Plus / EQ,
  Room Bar, Room Kit family, Room 55/70 family, Board Pro, Desk family) via
  the RoomOS xAPI over HTTPS. Standby, volume, mute, dial / hangup, DND,
  presentation, camera presets, on-screen messaging, reboot. State changes
  arrive instantly — the codec pushes them over HttpFeedback, with polling
  as the resync baseline.

source_url: https://roomos.cisco.com/print/TechDocs/HttpApi
tags: [cisco, webex, roomos, xapi, codec, room, board, desk, video-conferencing, vc]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [xapi_http]
ports: [443]
min_platform_version: "0.23.0"

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Cisco
    models:
      - Codec Pro
      - Codec Plus
      - Codec EQ
      - Room Bar
      - Room Bar Pro
      - Room Kit
      - Room Kit Mini
      - Room Kit EQ
      - Room Kit EQX
      - Room 55
      - Room 55 Dual
      - Room 70
      - Room 70 Single G2
      - Room 70 Dual G2
      - Room 70 G2
      - Room Panorama
      - Room 70 Panorama
      - Board Pro 55
      - Board Pro 75
      - Board Pro G2
      - Desk
      - Desk Mini
      - Desk Pro
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      All models share the same RoomOS xAPI surface; one driver covers the
      whole family. Verified against the xAPI documentation; no live-hardware
      verification yet. The xAPI has been stable across CE9 / RoomOS 10 / 11 /
      12 — minor command additions but the core surface used here predates CE9.

transport: http

help:
  overview: >
    Cisco Webex video-conferencing endpoints — the Codec Pro / Plus, Room Kit
    family, Room 55 / 70 series, Board Pro, and Desk Pro — all expose the
    same xAPI over HTTPS. This driver covers the controls an AV integrator
    actually wires to a touch panel: standby on / off, volume, mute, dial,
    hangup, do-not-disturb, presentation start / stop, camera presets, and
    on-screen messages. Standby, audio, DND, presentation, and occupancy
    changes are pushed by the codec the moment they happen (HttpFeedback);
    polling every 30 seconds keeps everything in sync as a fallback.
    xConfiguration writes are intentionally NOT included — settings belong
    in the Cisco web UI at install time, not on a control surface where
    they can be changed by accident.
  setup: >
    1. Set a static IP (or DHCP reservation) on the codec.
    2. In the codec's web UI (https://<codec-ip>) go to Users and create
       (or note) a local user with the "Admin" role — the default "admin"
       user works. Admin is what allows the codec to register instant push
       updates; a user with only the "Integrator" role still controls the
       codec, but state updates then arrive at poll speed. This driver
       uses HTTP Basic auth — SSO / single-sign-on users will not work.
    3. Confirm xAPI over HTTPS is enabled. In the web UI: Settings ->
       Configurations -> NetworkServices -> HTTP Mode. Default is
       HTTP+HTTPS, which is fine. (HTTP-only is also supported by toggling
       the Use HTTPS field on this device.)
    4. Add the codec in OpenAVC: enter the IP, leave port 443 / HTTPS on,
       enter the username and password from step 2.
    5. Push updates need the codec to reach the OpenAVC server over the
       network (it posts to OpenAVC's web port). If a firewall sits
       between them, allow that direction too. The Feedback Slot field
       only matters if another system also registers feedback on this
       codec: Cisco TMS uses slot 3, so pick a different one there.
    6. Polling refreshes system info, standby, audio, DND, presentation,
       and people-presence every 30 seconds as a resync baseline — with
       push active, panels update in about a second.

discovery:
  # The `_cisco-phone._tcp` candidate is widely associated with Cisco UC
  # IP phones (CUCM-registered handsets), not RoomOS video endpoints —
  # not safe to claim from this driver. Cisco RoomOS xAPI transport
  # docs (D15427.02) document HTTPS / SSH / WebSocket but say nothing
  # about mDNS advertisement. Home Assistant has no zeroconf-based
  # RoomOS integration — strong negative signal that no widely-known
  # stable mDNS string exists. Hint-only via legacy Tandberg OUI
  # (Cisco acquired Tandberg in 2009; codecs inherit it) plus the
  # general Cisco TelePresence MA-L block.
  oui:
    - "00:50:60"   # Tandberg Telecom AS — now Cisco Collaboration
    - "e8:0a:b9"   # Cisco Systems
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "cisco"
    - "tandberg"
    - "webex"

# Device-initiated push: the codec POSTs xStatus changes to a callback URL
# OpenAVC assigns (HttpFeedback webhooks). The register_feedback command in
# on_connect / polling hands the URL to the codec via {push_callback_url}.
push:
  type: http_listener

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 443
  ssl: true
  verify_ssl: false
  auth_type: "basic"
  username: "admin"
  password: ""
  timeout: 10.0
  poll_interval: 30
  feedback_slot: 1

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: Codec IP Address
    description: "IP address of the codec. Set a DHCP reservation on your network."
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 443
    label: HTTPS Port
    description: "443 by default. Use 80 if the codec is set to HTTP-only mode."
  ssl:
    type: boolean
    default: true
    label: Use HTTPS
    description: "Leave on. Disable only if the codec is in HTTP-only mode."
  verify_ssl:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Verify SSL Certificate
    description: "Codecs ship with self-signed certificates — leave off."
  username:
    type: string
    default: "admin"
    required: true
    label: Username
    description: "A local codec user with at least Integrator role."
  password:
    type: string
    default: ""
    required: true
    label: Password
    description: "Password for the user above."
    secret: true
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 30
    min: 5
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
    description: "Resync interval. Push feedback delivers changes instantly; polling is the fallback baseline."
  timeout:
    type: number
    default: 10.0
    label: Request Timeout (sec)
  feedback_slot:
    type: integer
    default: 1
    min: 1
    max: 4
    label: Feedback Slot (1-4)
    description: "Which of the codec's four HttpFeedback slots OpenAVC uses for push updates. Change it only if another system registers feedback on this codec — Cisco TMS uses slot 3."

state_variables:
  product_id:
    type: string
    label: Product ID
    help: "Marketing product name reported by the codec (e.g. 'Cisco Webex Codec Pro')."
  product_platform:
    type: string
    label: Product Platform
    help: "Hardware platform string (e.g. 'Codec Pro', 'Room Kit', 'Desk Pro')."
  software_version:
    type: string
    label: Software Version
    help: "RoomOS / CE software build, e.g. 'ce11.27.1.7'."
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
    help: "Codec serial number reported by xStatus SystemUnit Hardware Module SerialNumber."
  uptime_seconds:
    type: integer
    label: Uptime (sec)
    cloud_priority: low
    help: "Seconds since the codec last booted (xStatus SystemUnit Uptime)."
  standby_state:
    type: string
    label: Standby State
    control: true
    help: "Standby state from xStatus Standby State: Off / Standby / EnteringStandby / Halfwake."
  audio_volume:
    type: integer
    label: Volume (0-100)
    min: 0
    max: 100
    step: 1
    control: true
    help: "Speaker output volume, 0–100, from xStatus Audio Volume. 70 equals 0 dB gain."
  audio_volume_mute:
    type: string
    label: Output Mute
    control: true
    help: "Speaker mute state from xStatus Audio VolumeMute: On / Off."
  microphones_mute:
    type: string
    label: Microphone Mute
    control: true
    help: "Microphone mute state from xStatus Audio Microphones Mute: On / Off."
  dnd_state:
    type: string
    label: Do Not Disturb
    help: "Do-not-disturb state from xStatus Conference DoNotDisturb: Active / Inactive."
  presentation_mode:
    type: string
    label: Presentation Mode
    help: "Presentation pipeline state from xStatus Conference Presentation Mode: Sending / Receiving / Off."
  people_presence:
    type: string
    label: Room Occupied
    help: "People-presence detection from xStatus RoomAnalytics PeoplePresence: Yes / No / Unknown."
  people_count:
    type: integer
    label: People Count
    help: "Headcount from xStatus RoomAnalytics PeopleCount Current. -1 when unsupported or no signal."

# Headers used by every POST /putxml command. The /putxml endpoint requires
# Content-Type: text/xml — without it the codec rejects the body.
commands:

  # ── Push feedback registration ──────────────────────────────────────────
  # Registers OpenAVC's callback URL on the codec's feedback slot so xStatus
  # changes on the listed paths are POSTed the moment they happen (RoomOS 11
  # API guide, "Feedback from the device over HTTP"). Sent on connect and
  # repeated each poll cycle: registration is idempotent, and repeating it
  # re-activates a slot the codec shut off after failed deliveries. Requires
  # an Admin-role user. The expressions mirror the polled status paths —
  # never register the whole /Status tree (the guide warns a device in a
  # call produces more feedback than a controller should take).

  register_feedback:
    label: Register Push Feedback
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: '<Command><HttpFeedback><Register command="True"><FeedbackSlot>{feedback_slot}</FeedbackSlot><ServerUrl>{push_callback_url}</ServerUrl><Format>XML</Format><Expression item="1">/Status/Standby</Expression><Expression item="2">/Status/Audio/Volume</Expression><Expression item="3">/Status/Audio/VolumeMute</Expression><Expression item="4">/Status/Audio/Microphones/Mute</Expression><Expression item="5">/Status/Conference/DoNotDisturb</Expression><Expression item="6">/Status/Conference/Presentation/Mode</Expression><Expression item="7">/Status/RoomAnalytics/PeoplePresence</Expression><Expression item="8">/Status/RoomAnalytics/PeopleCount/Current</Expression></Register></HttpFeedback></Command>'
    help: "Points the codec's push feedback at OpenAVC. Runs automatically on connect and during polling — only needed manually after deregistering."

  deregister_feedback:
    label: Deregister Push Feedback
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: '<Command><HttpFeedback><Deregister command="True"><FeedbackSlot>{feedback_slot}</FeedbackSlot></Deregister></HttpFeedback></Command>'
    help: "Clears OpenAVC's feedback slot on the codec. Use before retiring this OpenAVC server so the codec stops posting to it (the next poll cycle re-registers while the device stays connected here)."

  # ── Standby ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  standby_activate:
    label: Standby On
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Standby><Activate/></Standby></Command>"
    help: "Put the codec to sleep."

  standby_deactivate:
    label: Standby Off (Wake)
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Standby><Deactivate/></Standby></Command>"
    help: "Wake the codec from standby."

  standby_halfwake:
    label: Standby Halfwake
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Standby><Halfwake/></Standby></Command>"
    help: "Drop the codec to half-wake (logo + welcome screen, instant resume)."

  # ── Audio: speaker volume + output mute ─────────────────────────────────

  audio_volume_set:
    label: Set Volume
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Volume><Set><Level>{level}</Level></Set></Volume></Audio></Command>"
    params:
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 50
        min: 0
        max: 100
        label: Level (0-100)

  audio_volume_increase:
    label: Volume +5
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Volume><Increase/></Volume></Audio></Command>"

  audio_volume_decrease:
    label: Volume -5
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Volume><Decrease/></Volume></Audio></Command>"

  audio_volume_mute:
    label: Output Mute On
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Volume><Mute/></Volume></Audio></Command>"

  audio_volume_unmute:
    label: Output Mute Off
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Volume><Unmute/></Volume></Audio></Command>"

  audio_volume_mute_toggle:
    label: Output Mute Toggle
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Volume><ToggleMute/></Volume></Audio></Command>"

  # ── Audio: microphone mute ──────────────────────────────────────────────

  audio_microphones_mute:
    label: Mic Mute On
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Microphones><Mute/></Microphones></Audio></Command>"

  audio_microphones_unmute:
    label: Mic Mute Off
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Microphones><Unmute/></Microphones></Audio></Command>"

  audio_microphones_mute_toggle:
    label: Mic Mute Toggle
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Audio><Microphones><ToggleMute/></Microphones></Audio></Command>"

  # ── Call control ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  query_call:
    label: Query Active Call
    method: GET
    path: "/getxml"
    query_params:
      location: "/Status/Call"
    help: "Returns the active-call status block. Empty if there are no active calls."

  dial:
    label: Dial
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Dial><Number>{number}</Number></Dial></Command>"
    help: >
      Dial a SIP URI (user@domain), H.323 alias, Webex meeting URL, or a Cisco
      Spark / Webex room. The codec decides protocol from the format of the
      number string.
    params:
      number:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: Number / SIP URI

  call_accept:
    label: Accept Incoming Call
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Call><Accept><CallId>{call_id}</CallId></Accept></Call></Command>"
    params:
      call_id:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "1"
        label: Call ID
        description: "Numeric call ID. Use Query Active Call to find current IDs."

  call_reject:
    label: Reject Incoming Call
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Call><Reject><CallId>{call_id}</CallId></Reject></Call></Command>"
    params:
      call_id:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "1"
        label: Call ID

  call_disconnect:
    label: Hang Up Call
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Call><Disconnect><CallId>{call_id}</CallId></Disconnect></Call></Command>"
    help: "Disconnect a specific call by CallId. Default '1' covers the common single-call case."
    params:
      call_id:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "1"
        label: Call ID

  call_hold:
    label: Hold Call
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Call><Hold><CallId>{call_id}</CallId></Hold></Call></Command>"
    params:
      call_id:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "1"
        label: Call ID

  call_resume:
    label: Resume Call
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Call><Resume><CallId>{call_id}</CallId></Resume></Call></Command>"
    params:
      call_id:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "1"
        label: Call ID

  # ── Conference: do not disturb ──────────────────────────────────────────

  dnd_activate:
    label: Do Not Disturb On
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Conference><DoNotDisturb><Activate><Timeout>{timeout}</Timeout></Activate></DoNotDisturb></Conference></Command>"
    help: "Block incoming calls and notifications for N minutes (1-20160, i.e. up to 14 days)."
    params:
      timeout:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 60
        min: 1
        max: 20160
        label: Timeout (minutes)

  dnd_deactivate:
    label: Do Not Disturb Off
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Conference><DoNotDisturb><Deactivate/></DoNotDisturb></Conference></Command>"

  # ── Presentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  presentation_start:
    label: Start Presentation (Share)
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Presentation><Start><PresentationSource>{source}</PresentationSource><SendingMode>{sending_mode}</SendingMode></Start></Presentation></Command>"
    help: >
      Share a connector (HDMI / USB-C input) into the call. PresentationSource
      is the connector ID (1, 2, 3 — match your codec's hardware). SendingMode
      'LocalRemote' shares to both far-end and local screen, 'LocalOnly' shows
      it on the local screen only.
    params:
      source:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 5
        label: Source Connector ID
      sending_mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["LocalRemote", "LocalOnly"]
        default: "LocalRemote"
        required: true
        label: Sending Mode

  presentation_stop:
    label: Stop Presentation
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Presentation><Stop/></Presentation></Command>"

  # ── Camera ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  camera_preset_activate:
    label: Recall Camera Preset
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Camera><Preset><Activate><PresetId>{preset_id}</PresetId></Activate></Preset></Camera></Command>"
    params:
      preset_id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 35
        label: Preset ID (1-35)

  camera_preset_store:
    label: Save Camera Preset
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Camera><Preset><Store><PresetId>{preset_id}</PresetId><CameraId>{camera_id}</CameraId><Name>{name}</Name><TakeSnapshot>True</TakeSnapshot></Store></Preset></Camera></Command>"
    help: "Save the current pan / tilt / zoom of the named camera as a preset."
    params:
      preset_id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 35
        label: Preset ID
      camera_id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 7
        label: Camera ID
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "Preset"
        label: Preset Name

  camera_position_set:
    label: Set Camera PTZ (Absolute)
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Camera><PositionSet><CameraId>{camera_id}</CameraId><Pan>{pan}</Pan><Tilt>{tilt}</Tilt><Zoom>{zoom}</Zoom></PositionSet></Camera></Command>"
    help: "Move the camera to absolute pan / tilt / zoom values. Ranges depend on the camera model."
    params:
      camera_id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 7
        label: Camera ID
      pan:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 0
        label: Pan
      tilt:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 0
        label: Tilt
      zoom:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 0
        label: Zoom

  camera_ramp:
    label: Camera Ramp (Continuous)
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Camera><Ramp><CameraId>{camera_id}</CameraId><Pan>{pan}</Pan><Tilt>{tilt}</Tilt><Zoom>{zoom}</Zoom></Ramp></Camera></Command>"
    help: >
      Start moving the camera continuously. Pan: Left / Right / Stop.
      Tilt: Up / Down / Stop. Zoom: In / Out / Stop. Always send Stop to
      halt motion (or use Camera Ramp Stop).
    params:
      camera_id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 7
        label: Camera ID
      pan:
        type: enum
        values: ["Stop", "Left", "Right"]
        default: "Stop"
        required: true
        label: Pan
      tilt:
        type: enum
        values: ["Stop", "Up", "Down"]
        default: "Stop"
        required: true
        label: Tilt
      zoom:
        type: enum
        values: ["Stop", "In", "Out"]
        default: "Stop"
        required: true
        label: Zoom

  camera_ramp_stop:
    label: Camera Ramp Stop
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><Camera><Ramp><CameraId>{camera_id}</CameraId><Pan>Stop</Pan><Tilt>Stop</Tilt><Zoom>Stop</Zoom></Ramp></Camera></Command>"
    help: "Stop all camera motion. Send when releasing a press-and-hold panel button."
    params:
      camera_id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        max: 7
        label: Camera ID

  # ── On-screen messaging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

  ui_alert_display:
    label: Show On-Screen Alert
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><UserInterface><Message><Alert><Display><Title>{title}</Title><Text>{text}</Text><Duration>{duration}</Duration></Display></Alert></Message></UserInterface></Command>"
    help: "Pop up a centered alert banner on the codec's screens. Duration in seconds (0 = until cleared)."
    params:
      title:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: "Notice"
        label: Title
      text:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: ""
        label: Message Text
      duration:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 10
        min: 0
        max: 3600
        label: Duration (sec)

  ui_alert_clear:
    label: Clear On-Screen Alert
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><UserInterface><Message><Alert><Clear/></Alert></Message></UserInterface></Command>"

  ui_textline_display:
    label: Show On-Screen Text Line
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><UserInterface><Message><TextLine><Display><Text>{text}</Text><Duration>{duration}</Duration></Display></TextLine></Message></UserInterface></Command>"
    help: "Tickertape-style text line. Useful for room-status feedback."
    params:
      text:
        type: string
        required: true
        default: ""
        label: Text
      duration:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 10
        min: 0
        max: 3600
        label: Duration (sec)

  ui_textline_clear:
    label: Clear On-Screen Text Line
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><UserInterface><Message><TextLine><Clear/></TextLine></Message></UserInterface></Command>"

  # ── System ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  system_reboot:
    label: Reboot Codec
    method: POST
    path: "/putxml"
    headers: { Content-Type: "text/xml" }
    body: "<Command><SystemUnit><Boot><Action>Restart</Action></Boot></SystemUnit></Command>"
    help: "Restart the codec. Takes 60-120 seconds to come back."

# Response patterns — shared by leaf poll replies AND HttpFeedback push
# bodies. Every tag test is written as <Name(?:\s[^>]*)?> because push
# bodies carry item="1" attributes on each element while poll replies may
# not; the (?:\s...) form also keeps <Volume> from swallowing <VolumeMute>.
# Push bodies additionally carry an <Identification> header block whose
# SystemName / MACAddress / SerialNumber / ProductID (uppercase D) / etc.
# must not shadow the payload — the serial rule requires the SystemUnit
# poll's <Module> parent, and <ProductId> (lowercase d) only exists in the
# SystemUnit poll body. First match wins, and with leaf-level polling every
# body contains exactly one target value.
responses:

  # SystemUnit (poll-only — metadata isn't registered for push)
  - match: '<ProductId(?:\s[^>]*)?>([^<]+)</ProductId>'
    set: { product_id: "$1" }
  - match: '<ProductPlatform(?:\s[^>]*)?>([^<]+)</ProductPlatform>'
    set: { product_platform: "$1" }
  - match: '<Software(?:\s[^>]*)?>\s*<Version(?:\s[^>]*)?>([^<]+)</Version>'
    set: { software_version: "$1" }
  - match: '<Module(?:\s[^>]*)?>\s*<SerialNumber(?:\s[^>]*)?>([^<]+)</SerialNumber>'
    set: { serial_number: "$1" }
  - match: '<Uptime(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\d+)</Uptime>'
    set: { uptime_seconds: "$1" }

  # Standby
  - match: '<Standby(?:\s[^>]*)?>\s*<State(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\w+)</State>'
    set: { standby_state: "$1" }

  # Audio — Microphones/Mute before the Volume rules keeps intent obvious;
  # the tag anchoring already prevents any cross-matching.
  - match: '<Microphones(?:\s[^>]*)?>\s*<Mute(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\w+)</Mute>'
    set: { microphones_mute: "$1" }
  - match: '<VolumeMute(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\w+)</VolumeMute>'
    set: { audio_volume_mute: "$1" }
  - match: '<Volume(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\d+)</Volume>'
    set: { audio_volume: "$1" }

  # Conference
  - match: '<DoNotDisturb(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\w+)</DoNotDisturb>'
    set: { dnd_state: "$1" }
  - match: '<Presentation(?:\s[^>]*)?>\s*<Mode(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\w+)</Mode>'
    set: { presentation_mode: "$1" }

  # Room analytics
  - match: '<PeoplePresence(?:\s[^>]*)?>(\w+)</PeoplePresence>'
    set: { people_presence: "$1" }
  - match: '<PeopleCount(?:\s[^>]*)?>\s*<Current(?:\s[^>]*)?>(-?\d+)</Current>'
    set: { people_count: "$1" }

# High-use parameterless actions surfaced as one-tap buttons.
quick_actions:
  - standby_deactivate
  - standby_activate
  - audio_microphones_mute_toggle
  - audio_volume_mute_toggle

# Leaf-level resync — one getxml location per state variable (raw paths, so
# each reply body matches exactly its rule; see the header note). The
# register_feedback repeat keeps the push registration alive: idempotent,
# and it re-activates a slot the codec deactivated after failed deliveries.
polling:
  queries:
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/ProductId"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/ProductPlatform"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/Software/Version"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/Hardware/Module/SerialNumber"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/Uptime"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/Standby"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/Audio/Volume"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/Audio/VolumeMute"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/Audio/Microphones/Mute"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/Conference/DoNotDisturb"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/Conference/Presentation/Mode"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/RoomAnalytics/PeoplePresence"
    - "/getxml?location=/Status/RoomAnalytics/PeopleCount/Current"
    - register_feedback

# Push registration first — the platform's listener is already up before
# on_connect runs, so no feedback body is missed — then the initial reads.
on_connect:
  - register_feedback
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/ProductId"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/ProductPlatform"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/Software/Version"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/Hardware/Module/SerialNumber"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/SystemUnit/Uptime"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/Standby"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/Audio/Volume"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/Audio/VolumeMute"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/Audio/Microphones/Mute"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/Conference/DoNotDisturb"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/Conference/Presentation/Mode"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/RoomAnalytics/PeoplePresence"
  - "/getxml?location=/Status/RoomAnalytics/PeopleCount/Current"

# ── SIMULATOR DEFINITION ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The auto-simulator answers GET /getxml?location=... and POST /putxml. Body
# is appended after a "|" delimiter so the handlers can match it. The XML we
# emit mirrors the real codec: leaf getxml replies wrap the value from the
# root with item="1" attributes, and push feedback bodies (the notifications
# templates below, POSTed to the URL captured from HttpFeedback Register)
# carry the same wrapping plus an <Identification> header block — so the
# driver's attribute-tolerance and Identification-shadowing anchors are
# exercised end to end.
simulator:
  initial_state:
    product_id: "Cisco Webex Codec Pro"
    product_platform: "Codec Pro"
    software_version: "ce11.27.1.7"
    serial_number: "FCH99999SIM"
    uptime_seconds: 432000
    standby_state: "Off"
    audio_volume: 50
    audio_volume_mute: "Off"
    microphones_mute: "Off"
    dnd_state: "Inactive"
    presentation_mode: "Off"
    people_presence: "No"
    people_count: 0
    feedback_url: ""

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02

  # Cisco-shaped push bodies (Identification block included on purpose —
  # its SerialNumber/ProductID must not cross-write other state vars).
  notifications:
    standby_state:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><Standby item="1"><State item="1">{value}</State></Standby></Status>'
    audio_volume:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><Audio item="1"><Volume item="1">{value}</Volume></Audio></Status>'
    audio_volume_mute:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><Audio item="1"><VolumeMute item="1">{value}</VolumeMute></Audio></Status>'
    microphones_mute:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><Audio item="1"><Microphones item="1"><Mute item="1">{value}</Mute></Microphones></Audio></Status>'
    dnd_state:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><Conference item="1"><DoNotDisturb item="1">{value}</DoNotDisturb></Conference></Status>'
    presentation_mode:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><Conference item="1"><Presentation item="1"><Mode item="1">{value}</Mode></Presentation></Conference></Status>'
    people_presence:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><RoomAnalytics item="1"><PeoplePresence item="1">{value}</PeoplePresence></RoomAnalytics></Status>'
    people_count:
      "*": '<Status><Identification><SystemName>Sim Room</SystemName><SerialNumber>FCH99999SIM</SerialNumber><ProductID>Cisco Webex Codec Pro</ProductID></Identification><RoomAnalytics item="1"><PeopleCount item="1"><Current item="1">{value}</Current></PeopleCount></RoomAnalytics></Status>'

  controls:
    - type: indicator
      key: product_id
      label: Product
    - type: indicator
      key: product_platform
      label: Platform
    - type: indicator
      key: software_version
      label: Software
    - type: indicator
      key: serial_number
      label: Serial
    - type: slider
      key: uptime_seconds
      label: Uptime (sec)
      min: 0
      max: 9999999
    - type: select
      key: standby_state
      label: Standby
      options: ["Off", "Standby", "EnteringStandby", "Halfwake"]
    - type: slider
      key: audio_volume
      label: Volume
      min: 0
      max: 100
    - type: select
      key: audio_volume_mute
      label: Output Mute
      options: ["Off", "On"]
    - type: select
      key: microphones_mute
      label: Mic Mute
      options: ["Off", "On"]
    - type: select
      key: dnd_state
      label: DND
      options: ["Inactive", "Active"]
    - type: select
      key: presentation_mode
      label: Presentation
      options: ["Off", "Sending", "Receiving"]
    - type: select
      key: people_presence
      label: Occupied
      options: ["Yes", "No", "Unknown"]
    - type: slider
      key: people_count
      label: People Count
      min: -1
      max: 50
    - type: indicator
      key: feedback_url
      label: Push Feedback URL

  command_handlers:

    # ── POST /putxml — HttpFeedback registration ─────────────────────────
    # Captures the ServerUrl the controller registers; state changes are
    # then POSTed there (see notifications above). The URL is surfaced in
    # the Simulator UI so a live test can confirm the registration landed.

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><HttpFeedback><Register command="True"><FeedbackSlot>(\d+)</FeedbackSlot><ServerUrl>([^<]+)</ServerUrl>.*'
      handler: |
        state["feedback_url"] = match.group(2)
        register_callback(match.group(2))
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><HttpFeedbackRegisterResult status="OK"><FeedbackSlot>' + match.group(1) + '</FeedbackSlot></HttpFeedbackRegisterResult></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><HttpFeedback><Deregister command="True"><FeedbackSlot>(\d+)</FeedbackSlot>.*'
      handler: |
        unregister_callback(state["feedback_url"])
        state["feedback_url"] = ""
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><HttpFeedbackDeregisterResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # ── GET /getxml?location=... (leaf locations, matching the driver's
    #    polling list; replies wrap the value from the root with item
    #    attributes like the real codec) ────────────────────────────────

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/SystemUnit/ProductId\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><SystemUnit item="1"><ProductId item="1">{state["product_id"]}</ProductId></SystemUnit></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/SystemUnit/ProductPlatform\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><SystemUnit item="1"><ProductPlatform item="1">{state["product_platform"]}</ProductPlatform></SystemUnit></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/SystemUnit/Software/Version\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><SystemUnit item="1"><Software item="1"><Version item="1">{state["software_version"]}</Version></Software></SystemUnit></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/SystemUnit/Hardware/Module/SerialNumber\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><SystemUnit item="1"><Hardware item="1"><Module item="1"><SerialNumber item="1">{state["serial_number"]}</SerialNumber></Module></Hardware></SystemUnit></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/SystemUnit/Uptime\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><SystemUnit item="1"><Uptime item="1">{state["uptime_seconds"]}</Uptime></SystemUnit></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Standby\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><Standby item="1"><State item="1">{state["standby_state"]}</State></Standby></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Audio/Volume\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><Audio item="1"><Volume item="1">{state["audio_volume"]}</Volume></Audio></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Audio/VolumeMute\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><Audio item="1"><VolumeMute item="1">{state["audio_volume_mute"]}</VolumeMute></Audio></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Audio/Microphones/Mute\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><Audio item="1"><Microphones item="1"><Mute item="1">{state["microphones_mute"]}</Mute></Microphones></Audio></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Conference/DoNotDisturb\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><Conference item="1"><DoNotDisturb item="1">{state["dnd_state"]}</DoNotDisturb></Conference></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Conference/Presentation/Mode\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><Conference item="1"><Presentation item="1"><Mode item="1">{state["presentation_mode"]}</Mode></Presentation></Conference></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/RoomAnalytics/PeoplePresence\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><RoomAnalytics item="1"><PeoplePresence item="1">{state["people_presence"]}</PeoplePresence></RoomAnalytics></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/RoomAnalytics/PeopleCount/Current\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(f'<?xml version="1.0"?><Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4"><RoomAnalytics item="1"><PeopleCount item="1"><Current item="1">{state["people_count"]}</Current></PeopleCount></RoomAnalytics></Status>')

    - match: '^GET /getxml\?location=/?Status/Call\b.*'
      handler: |
        respond(
          '<?xml version="1.0"?>'
          '<Status product="Cisco Codec" version="ce26.0.0" apiVersion="4">'
          '</Status>'
        )

    # ── POST /putxml — xCommand handlers ─────────────────────────────────

    # Standby
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Standby><Activate.*'
      handler: |
        state["standby_state"] = "Standby"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><StandbyActivateResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Standby><Deactivate.*'
      handler: |
        state["standby_state"] = "Off"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><StandbyDeactivateResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Standby><Halfwake.*'
      handler: |
        state["standby_state"] = "Halfwake"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><StandbyHalfwakeResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Audio volume
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Volume><Set><Level>(\d+)</Level>.*'
      handler: |
        level = max(0, min(100, int(match.group(1))))
        state["audio_volume"] = level
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><VolumeSetResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Volume><Increase.*'
      handler: |
        state["audio_volume"] = min(100, int(state["audio_volume"]) + 5)
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><VolumeIncreaseResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Volume><Decrease.*'
      handler: |
        state["audio_volume"] = max(0, int(state["audio_volume"]) - 5)
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><VolumeDecreaseResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Volume><Mute.*'
      handler: |
        state["audio_volume_mute"] = "On"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><VolumeMuteResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Volume><Unmute.*'
      handler: |
        state["audio_volume_mute"] = "Off"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><VolumeUnmuteResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Volume><ToggleMute.*'
      handler: |
        state["audio_volume_mute"] = "Off" if state["audio_volume_mute"] == "On" else "On"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><VolumeToggleMuteResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Microphone mute
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Microphones><Mute.*'
      handler: |
        state["microphones_mute"] = "On"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><MicrophonesMuteResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Microphones><Unmute.*'
      handler: |
        state["microphones_mute"] = "Off"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><MicrophonesUnmuteResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Audio><Microphones><ToggleMute.*'
      handler: |
        state["microphones_mute"] = "Off" if state["microphones_mute"] == "On" else "On"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><MicrophonesToggleMuteResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Call control — sim acks every variant; no call-state machine
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Dial>.*'
      handler: |
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><DialResult status="OK"><CallId>1</CallId></DialResult></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Call><(?:Accept|Reject|Disconnect|Hold|Resume)>.*'
      handler: |
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><CallResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Conference
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Conference><DoNotDisturb><Activate.*'
      handler: |
        state["dnd_state"] = "Active"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><DoNotDisturbActivateResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Conference><DoNotDisturb><Deactivate.*'
      handler: |
        state["dnd_state"] = "Inactive"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><DoNotDisturbDeactivateResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Presentation
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Presentation><Start>.*'
      handler: |
        state["presentation_mode"] = "Sending"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><PresentationStartResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Presentation><Stop.*'
      handler: |
        state["presentation_mode"] = "Off"
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><PresentationStopResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Camera — sim acks; no PTZ state mirrored
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><Camera>.*'
      handler: |
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><CameraResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # User interface messaging — sim acks
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><UserInterface>.*'
      handler: |
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><UserInterfaceResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Reboot — sim acks (does not actually go offline)
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command><SystemUnit><Boot>.*'
      handler: |
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><BootResult status="OK"/></Command>')

    # Catch-all for any other xCommand we did not enumerate
    - match: '^POST /putxml\|<Command>.*'
      handler: |
        respond('<?xml version="1.0"?><Command><Result status="OK"/></Command>')
